From: OpenCode <opencode@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7615: fail MT7663 init cleanly on invalid EEPROM data

Avoid hard hangs during WL-WN575A3 bring-up by refusing to continue MT7663
registration when the EEPROM-derived txpower data is unusable. Return a
probe error instead of progressing into unstable radio initialization.

Signed-off-by: OpenCode <opencode@local>

--- a/mt7615/pci_init.c
+++ b/mt7615/pci_init.c
@@ -84,8 +84,13 @@
 		return ret;
 
 	ret = mt7615_init_hardware(dev);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		if (is_mt7663(&dev->mt76))
+			dev_err(dev->mt76.dev,
+				"mt7663 init aborted: EEPROM/txpower init failed (%d)\n",
+				ret);
 		return ret;
+	}
 
 	ret = mt76_register_device(&dev->mt76, true, mt76_rates,
 				   ARRAY_SIZE(mt76_rates));
